From: Project Arctic
Subject: win32u: a maximized window waits for the monitors before it fills them again.

When the display changes (a game's mode, its end), every maximized window
is told to fill its monitor's work area again (ARCTIC_SW_REMAXIMIZE, patch
0112), each in its own thread. The display driver counts the monitors anew
on each change, and for a moment there are none: a window that came to it
then got an empty work area and the smallest size a frame has, 136x33 at
the top left, and stayed so, still maximized. After CS2 the IDE was gone
from the screen that way. Now a window waits for its place to be known
again (a work area, and a maximized size at least half of it), 10 ms at a
time for up to half a second, and leaves the window alone if it never is.
---
--- a/dlls/win32u/window.c	2026-11-23 19:23:48.340115400 +0100
+++ b/dlls/win32u/window.c	2026-11-23 19:23:57.747115100 +0100
@@ -5046,12 +5046,38 @@
                         info.ptMaxSize.y, SWP_NOZORDER | SWP_NOACTIVATE | SWP_FRAMECHANGED );
 }
 
+/* Arctic: where a maximized window goes is known only while the screen has
+ * its monitors: the display driver counts them again on each change of mode,
+ * and in between there is no monitor and no work area. A window remaximized
+ * then took the smallest size a frame has (136x33 at the top left, under
+ * the taskbar) and kept it: after CS2 changed the mode, the maximized IDE was
+ * out of sight, still maximized, and its taskbar button only minimized and
+ * restored the strip (2026-11-23). */
+static BOOL maximized_place_known( HWND hwnd, const MINMAXINFO *info )
+{
+    RECT rc_max;
+
+    if (!get_maximized_rect( hwnd, &rc_max )) return FALSE;
+    if (rc_max.right - rc_max.left <= 0 || rc_max.bottom - rc_max.top <= 0) return FALSE;
+    /* the work area is there, but the desktop the default comes from not yet */
+    return info->ptMaxSize.x * 2 >= rc_max.right - rc_max.left && info->ptMaxSize.y * 2 >= rc_max.bottom - rc_max.top;
+}
+
 /* Arctic: ... and only if it is somewhere else now */
 static void remaximize_if_moved( HWND hwnd )
 {
     MINMAXINFO info = get_min_max_info( hwnd );
     RECT rect;
 
+    /* the monitors are being counted again: a moment later, up to half a second */
+    for (int tries = 0; !maximized_place_known( hwnd, &info ); tries++)
+    {
+        LARGE_INTEGER timeout = { .QuadPart = -100000 };   /* 10 ms */
+
+        if (tries == 50) return;   /* no monitor for good: the window stays as it is */
+        NtDelayExecution( FALSE, &timeout );
+        info = get_min_max_info( hwnd );
+    }
     get_window_rect( hwnd, &rect, get_thread_dpi() );
     if (rect.left == info.ptMaxPosition.x && rect.top == info.ptMaxPosition.y &&
         rect.right - rect.left == info.ptMaxSize.x && rect.bottom - rect.top == info.ptMaxSize.y)
